From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer, shell32: virtual desktops, Task View and Alt+Tab

Several desktops, as Windows 10 has them, on the cloaking of patch 0067.

- explorer (vdesktop.c): each application window -- what gets a taskbar
  button -- belongs to a desktop, its owned windows with it; the shell's own
  surfaces and tool windows are on every desktop. Switching shell-cloaks the
  other desktops' windows (still visible to their programs) and activates
  the new desktop's top window; a new window opens on the current desktop;
  activating a window on another desktop (a program, a notification) goes
  there. Win+Ctrl+D adds a desktop, Win+Ctrl+Left/Right switch, Win+Ctrl+F4
  closes the current one (its windows move to a neighbour),
  Win+Ctrl+Shift+Left/Right carry the active window along, and a brief
  indicator names the desktop. Alt+Tab (Shift+Alt+Tab back) shows the
  current desktop's windows, most recently used first, with thumbnails;
  releasing Alt switches (a low-level keyboard hook while it is up),
  Escape cancels.
  Task View (Win+Tab, or the new button beside Start): the desktops in a
  strip across the top, each a scaled map of its windows, with New desktop;
  the windows as thumbnails -- hovering a desktop shows its windows; click
  to switch or to activate; drag a window onto a desktop, or use its menu
  (Move to, Show this window on all desktops, Close); Escape, arrows, Enter
  and Delete. Thumbnails are taken from the screen while a window is the
  foreground one: there is no cross-process PrintWindow in Wine, and a
  cloaked window has no pixels on the screen.
  State is where Windows keeps it, HKCU\...\Explorer\VirtualDesktops
  (VirtualDesktopIDs, CurrentVirtualDesktop, Desktops\{id}\Name); a
  window's desktop is its root owner's "__sg_vdesk" property. The taskbar
  shows the current desktop's windows. Other processes drive it with the
  registered message "SgVirtualDesktopCommand" to Shell_TrayWnd.
- shell32: IVirtualDesktopManager (CLSID_VirtualDesktopManager), the
  documented interface programs use: IsWindowOnCurrentVirtualDesktop,
  GetWindowDesktopId, and MoveWindowToDesktop for the caller's own windows
  (E_ACCESSDENIED for another program's, as on Windows). Declared in
  shobjidl.idl from its published IIDs.

Gate: test/vdesk-gate.sh.
